WasmFS: open(O_CREAT) ignores the parent directory's write permission

A file could be created in a directory without write permission, where
mkdir(), unlink() and rename() already refuse with EACCES.

Upstream: https://github.com/emscripten-core/emscripten/issues/18033 (open)
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-create-permission.md

diff --git a/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp b/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp
index 8d098b1..46f0caf 100644
--- a/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp
+++ b/system/lib/wasmfs/syscalls.cpp
@@ -475,7 +475,9 @@ static __wasi_fd_t doOpen(path::ParsedParent parsed,
         backend = parent->getBackend();
       }
 
-      // TODO: Check write permissions on the parent directory.
+      if (!(lockedParent.getMode() & WASMFS_PERM_WRITE)) {
+        return -EACCES;
+      }
       std::shared_ptr<File> created;
       if (backend == parent->getBackend()) {
         created = lockedParent.insertDataFile(std::string(childName), mode);
